.TH elfshaker-gc 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-gc \- Cleanup redundant snapshots and unreferenced objects. This frees up disk space after creating a pack.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker gc\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-loose\-snapshots\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-loose\-objects\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Cleanup redundant snapshots and unreferenced objects. This frees up disk space after creating a pack.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Do not actually delete anything.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-loose\-snapshots\fR
Delete redundant loose snapshots which exist an a pack.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-loose\-objects\fR
Delete unreferenced loose objects (which are not needed by any snapshot).
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enables verbose description of the execution process.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Set the path to the elfshaker repository.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
